# Paddle sandbox API key for the `paddle-sandbox` MCP server.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your key — `.env` is gitignored.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The two Paddle MCP servers authenticate differently:
#
# | MCP server     | URL                                | Authentication          |
# | -------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
# | paddle-sandbox | https://sandbox-mcp.paddle.com/mcp | PADDLE_SANDBOX_API_KEY  |
# | paddle-live    | https://mcp.paddle.com/mcp         | OAuth (browser sign-in) |
#
# `paddle-live` uses OAuth, so there is no live key to set here.
#
# Generate a sandbox key at Paddle > Developer tools > Authentication:
#   https://sandbox-vendors.paddle.com/authentication-v2
#
# Sandbox keys are prefixed `pdl_sdbx_`. Grant only the scopes you need; for
# full coverage of these skills: product.write, price.write,
# customer.read/write, subscription.read/write, transaction.read,
# notification.write.
#
# IMPORTANT: set this with NO space around the `=`.
#   export PADDLE_SANDBOX_API_KEY=pdl_sdbx_...     correct
#   export PADDLE_SANDBOX_API_KEY= pdl_sdbx_...    sets it to EMPTY, silently
#
# The MCP server reads this from the process environment of whatever launches
# your editor, not from this file — so also export it in your shell profile,
# or use direnv, then restart the editor.

PADDLE_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
